          "question": "Is there a questionnaire they use for it?",
          "answer": "The condition is clear from your first message: you described anxiety most days that affects your work, so I've taken \"it\" to mean anxiety.\n\nThe most commonly used tool is the **seven-item generalized anxiety disorder questionnaire (GAD-7)**. Clinicians use it both to screen for the condition and to track how severe it is over time. Scores fall into bands: 5 is mild, 10 is moderate, and 15 is severe. A score of 10 or more is the usual point at which further assessment follows. (Source: \"Generalized anxiety disorder: screening instruments and first-line care\")\n\nMy search returned only this one tool. It does not describe what the individual questions cover, so I can't say more about its content. A clinician can explain it and tell you whether it fits your situation.\n\nThis tool is a screening aid, not a diagnosis. Only a clinician can interpret a score in the context of your full history.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n[sources: guideline-anxiety-screening-and-first-line-care]",
